# A note export builds a whole HTML document from the note's own fields and
# hands it to `exportToPDF`, which drops it into a hidden frame by assigning
# `iframe.srcdoc` and calling `print()`. The frame carries no `sandbox`
# attribute, so it keeps the embedder's origin and the markup's own scripts
# run with `window.parent` in reach -- on the desktop build that parent is an
# Electron renderer, which turns stored markup in a note title into code
# execution. The fixed revision sandboxes the frame (`iframe.sandbox.add(...)`, keeping
# only `allow-same-origin` and `allow-modals`, so script execution is
# withheld) and, in the template builder, escapes the note fields before
# interpolating them; either control alone stops the markup from reaching a
# parser that can run it.
#
# `srcdoc` is the inline-markup sibling of the `contentDocument.write` route
# the same concept covers, and the same two controls apply. Over
# 662 TypeScript/TSX files of the application (apps/web/src, packages/core/src
# and packages/editor/src) the unpatched revision reports 2 VYQL-INJ-243 rows
# against the patched revision's 1: the export frame above disappears, the
# other frame is a download helper that assigns `srcdoc` in the same
# unsandboxed shape and is unchanged at both revisions. The JSX embed frame in
# packages/editor, which passes `sandbox={getSandboxFeatures(src)}` beside its
# `srcDoc`, reports on neither revision.

test "rank1469: an export frame's srcdoc is assigned unsandboxed markup"
  lang javascript
  file apps/web/src/common/export.ts
  expect VYQL-INJ-243
  expect_review code.UnsanitizedFrameDocumentWrite
  code
  ```
  export async function exportToPDF(
    title: string,
    content: string
  ): Promise<boolean> {
    if (!content) return false;

    return new Promise<boolean>((resolve) => {
      const iframe = document.createElement("iframe");

      iframe.srcdoc = content;
      iframe.style.position = "fixed";
      iframe.style.width = "0";
      iframe.style.height = "0";
      iframe.loading = "eager";

      iframe.onload = async () => {
        if (!iframe.contentWindow) return;
        if (iframe.contentDocument) iframe.contentDocument.title = title;
        iframe.contentWindow.print();
      };

      document.body.appendChild(iframe);
    });
  }
  ```

test "rank1469: an export frame is sandboxed before its srcdoc is assigned"
  lang javascript
  file apps/web/src/common/export.ts
  reject VYQL-INJ-243
  reject_review code.UnsanitizedFrameDocumentWrite
  code
  ```
  export async function exportToPDF(
    title: string,
    content: string
  ): Promise<boolean> {
    if (!content) return false;

    return new Promise<boolean>((resolve) => {
      const iframe = document.createElement("iframe");

      iframe.srcdoc = content;
      iframe.style.position = "fixed";
      iframe.style.width = "0";
      iframe.style.height = "0";
      iframe.loading = "eager";
      iframe.sandbox.add("allow-same-origin", "allow-modals");

      iframe.onload = async () => {
        if (!iframe.contentWindow) return;
        if (iframe.contentDocument) iframe.contentDocument.title = title;
        iframe.contentWindow.print();
      };

      document.body.appendChild(iframe);
    });
  }
  ```

